  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7265114aa1e7f41ada19d74a427f9e13, type: 3}
  m_Name: BrickBreakerCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: xpTURN.Feedback.Samples::xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.SampleCard
  Title: Showcase
  Try: Break all 32 bricks (the top rows crack first), then beat the boss. Keep breaking
    within two seconds to build a combo; press 3 to go straight to the boss. Turn
    the feedback off to see the same game plain.
  See: 'The board moves the ball itself on the game clock (no physics) and never
    waits for a feedback. One Impact a frame carries the combo tier as its intensity:
    the camera shake grows, the hit stops and the rumble come in by intensity range.
    The score counts up on the unscaled clock; a floating +score needs TMP Essential
    Resources. The boss comes down with a tween from above its place, a hit stops
    the game for 0.15 s (a 0.5 s guard keeps the flashes under the limit), its bar
    trails, a red pulse runs while it rages, and its defeat slows time and drains
    the colour. Before plays the same game with no feedback and no floating scores.'
  Controls: "\u2190 \u2192 \xB7 A D \xB7 Z X \xB7 Left stick \xB7 D-pad \u2014 paddle
    \xB7 Mouse \u2014 paddle \xB7 click to launch \xB7 Space \xB7 1 \xB7 Gamepad
    South \u2014 launch \xB7 2 \xB7 Gamepad West \u2014 restart \xB7 3 \xB7 Gamepad
    North \u2014 boss now"
  SceneGuid: cffdef758879a44fca292250db732551
  SceneName: BrickBreaker
  RequiredType: xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.Showcase.BrickBreakerLab, xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.Showcase.BrickBreaker
  RequiresText: the Particle System module
  OpenInEditor: 0
